      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: Fit COBRA on the targeted-panel expression for our 300 COPD patients, with smoking pack-years and age as numeric covariates in a design table keyed by the same patient IDs. I'm not sure whether the lab ran the 250-gene panel or the 2,000-gene panel.\nUser follow-up: It was the 2,000-gene panel."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"Fit COBRA on the targeted-panel expression for our 300 COPD patients, with smoking pack-years and age as numeric covariates in a design table keyed by the same patient IDs.\" -- available from COBRA's output plus a step you run outside NetZoo: Pass adjusted_coexpression to PANDA, PUMA or OTTER (registered handoff) after identifier checks.\n2. \"I'm not sure whether the lab ran the 250-gene panel or the 2,000-gene panel.\" -- not matched to any registered workflow.\n\nSelected path: **COBRA**.\n\n**COBRA** — Model covariate-associated gene co-expression with COBRA. COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Correcting gene means alone may leave covariance confounding. Covariate-associated components are not TF-to-gene regulatory edges or proof that a covariate causes the expression pattern.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `expression_file`: expression matrix\n- `design_file`: sample covariate design matrix\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `coexpression_network`: Inferred gene-to-gene associations.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nInput compatibility has not been assessed: your data was not checked against the workflow's required inputs; name your input files to have them checked. This is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: Previous NetZoo goal: Fit COBRA on the targeted-panel expression for our 300 COPD patients, with smoking pack-years and age as numeric covariates in a design table keyed by the same patient IDs. I'm not sure whether the lab ran the 250-gene panel or the 2,000-gene panel.\nUser follow-up: It was the 2,000-gene panel.\nUser follow-up: Sorry, I checked again: it was the 250-gene panel."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Routing matched these registered workflows to your words, but the capability check did not confirm that any of them gives what you asked for:\n- **PANDA** — produces: One weighted TF-to-gene regulatory network across all the samples given.\n- **PUMA** — produces: One weighted network of how TFs and miRNAs regulate genes, across all samples.\n- **LIONESS-PANDA** — produces: One TF-gene network per sample, plus the aggregate network.\n- **LIONESS-PUMA** — produces: One TF/miRNA-gene network per sample, plus the aggregate network.\n- **OTTER** — produces: One weighted TF-to-gene regulatory network across all samples, fitted so that it agrees with the PPI network and gene co-expression.\n- **GIRAFFE** — produces: A signed TF-to-gene regulatory matrix (positive activating, negative repressing), across all samples. Each TF's activity in each sample, estimated apart from its own mRNA level.\n\nCompare what each produces with what you asked for. Ask again to re-run the check, or say which result you want and from which workflow.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
